PART III — USE-BASED RESTRICTIONS (Attachment A)
================================================================================

You agree not to use the Release or any Derivative Work, in whole or in
part, for any of the following purposes ("Prohibited Uses"):

A.  STANDARD OPENRAIL PROHIBITED USES

  1. To violate any applicable national, federal, state, local, or
     international law or regulation;
  2. To exploit or harm minors in any way, including the generation of
     child sexual abuse material;
  3. To generate, propagate, or facilitate verifiably false information
     or content with the aim of harming others;
  4. To generate, propagate, or facilitate personal identifiable
     information that can be used to harm an individual;
  5. To defame, disparage, or otherwise harass others;
  6. To generate, propagate, or facilitate fully automated decision-making
     that adversely impacts an individual's legal rights or creates or
     modifies a binding, enforceable obligation;
  7. To generate, propagate, or facilitate any use intended to or which
     has the effect of discriminating against or harming individuals or
     groups based on protected legal characteristics;
  8. To exploit any of the vulnerabilities of a specific group of
     persons based on age, social, physical, or mental characteristics
     in order to materially distort the behaviour of a person pertaining
     to that group in a manner that causes or is likely to cause that
     person physical or psychological harm;
  9. To provide medical advice or medical-results interpretation;
  10.To generate or disseminate information for the purpose of
     administering justice, law enforcement, immigration, or asylum
     processes, such as predicting an individual will commit fraud or
     other criminal activity;
  11.To facilitate or carry out mass surveillance, including the
     deployment of facial-recognition or biometric systems against
     individuals without their consent or in violation of applicable
     law;
  12.To generate or facilitate the generation of code that constitutes
     a piece of malware, ransomware, a virus, a worm, a trojan, a
     keylogger, a spyware payload, a rootkit, a botnet command-and-
     control component, a credential harvester, an exploit for a known
     or unknown vulnerability, or any similar artefact intended for
     unauthorised access to or damage to information systems.

B.  CUSTOM USE-BASED RESTRICTIONS — ABLITERATION STUDIES

  13.To remove, weaken or bypass the safety behaviour of a model in order
     to deploy it for, or offer it as a service for, any Prohibited Use in
     section A;
  14.To use the Release to generate any content described in section A,
     outside a documented safety-evaluation, red-teaming or
     academic-research context.

